WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.497
It was a beautiful Sunday morning.

2
00:00:14.498 --> 00:00:18.469
Paula, Becky, and Helen were waiting for their mother.

3
00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:21.829
"Good morning, girls!" said Dad.

4
00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:26.098
"Good morning, Dad!" said the girls.

5
00:00:26.099 --> 00:00:29.880
Dad began to hum as he put on Mom's pink apron.

6
00:00:29.881 --> 00:00:33.259
"Where's Mom?" asked Paula.

7
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.318
"Your mother is sick," said Dad.

8
00:00:36.319 --> 00:00:40.472
"So today, I'm going to make your breakfast!"

9
00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:44.430
Every Sunday, Mom made a big breakfast for the family.

10
00:00:44.431 --> 00:00:46.682
Mom was a wonderful cook.

11
00:00:46.683 --> 00:00:51.706
The family would talk and laugh as they ate their breakfast together.

12
00:00:51.707 --> 00:00:54.957
"What would you like to have?" asked Dad.

13
00:00:54.958 --> 00:00:58.459
"Can I have some pancakes?" asked Becky.

14
00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:03.293
"I'd like scrambled eggs and some toast," said Helen.

15
00:01:03.294 --> 00:01:08.435
"May I have some bacon and sausage?" asked Paula.

16
00:01:08.436 --> 00:01:12.657
"Uh . . . okay. Sure, no problem!"

17
00:01:12.658 --> 00:01:16.151
"Dad, can we help?" asked Helen.

18
00:01:16.152 --> 00:01:18.474
"No, thank you."

19
00:01:18.475 --> 00:01:21.092
Dad put the frying pan on the stove.

20
00:01:21.093 --> 00:01:24.114
He put two pieces of bread into the toaster.

21
00:01:24.115 --> 00:01:27.241
"Now for the pancakes!"

22
00:01:27.242 --> 00:01:32.005
Dad looked in the drawers, in the refrigerator, and under the sink.

23
00:01:32.006 --> 00:01:36.308
"Where does your mother hide the pancake mix?"

24
00:01:36.309 --> 00:01:39.006
Dad scratched his head.

25
00:01:39.007 --> 00:01:44.522
"Mom usually keeps it in the pantry." Becky pointed.

26
00:01:44.523 --> 00:01:48.802
"Dad! The frying pan!" screamed Helen.

27
00:01:48.803 --> 00:01:52.710
Dad put the bacon and sausage into the smoking pan.

28
00:01:52.711 --> 00:02:00.766
Then he put some pancake mix into a bowl and cracked two eggs.

29
00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:05.512
Ding! The toaster popped up two pieces of black toast.

30
00:02:05.513 --> 00:02:09.180
"Dad, the toast . . . ," said Helen.

31
00:02:09.181 --> 00:02:13.111
"Dad, the bacon . . . ," said Paula.

32
00:02:13.112 --> 00:02:17.669
"Oh no!" shouted Dad.

33
00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:21.937
The girls began to giggle.

34
00:02:21.938 --> 00:02:24.166
"How does your mother do it?

35
00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:26.615
I never knew cooking was so hard!

36
00:02:26.616 --> 00:02:32.627
I'm sorry, girls, but I messed up our big breakfast," said Dad.

37
00:02:32.628 --> 00:02:35.790
The girls ran over and hugged their dad.

38
00:02:35.791 --> 00:02:38.009
"That's okay, Dad.

39
00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:42.335
We can have cereal!" said the girls.

40
00:02:42.336 --> 00:02:44.097
Paula got the milk.

41
00:02:44.098 --> 00:02:45.914
Becky got the cereal.

42
00:02:45.915 --> 00:02:48.529
Helen got the bowls and spoons.

43
00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:54.941
Having a big breakfast wasn't as important as being together.
